WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.190
- Since you will all be touring together,

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.520
I have to ask, do any of you have like,

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.160
good luck rituals, like before,

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.410
do you have any, are you superstitious?

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.520
Any things you have to do
before you go on stage?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.300
I'll start with Rona.
Let's start with Rona.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.990
- Well, yeah, we do.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.060
Before we go out, we look at each other,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.507
we give each other a thumbs up and we say,

00:00:16.507 --> 00:00:18.010
"Have fun with your friends."

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.260
- Oh, that's amazing!

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.187
I'm stealing that one, okay,

00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:24.020
that's stolen.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.000
- Well we stole it too.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.833
- Okay, I was like,

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:26.666
"That is officially stolen."

00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:27.580
- We were in Europe

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.460
when we first heard someone say that

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.827
and it was just, we were like,

00:00:30.827 --> 00:00:32.674
"Oh no, that's it."

00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:33.981
We're gonna have fun with our friends.

00:00:33.981 --> 00:00:34.814
- Yeah, 'cause no matter what going

00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:35.647
on in life or anything,

00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:36.480
it's just alright,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.320
yeah that's nice, I love that.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.510
Do y'all have any?

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.890
- We have a bunch of individual rituals,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.870
but I think we get together
in a little huddle,

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.170
similar to the ladies,
but Danny will always say,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.530
what do you say, Danny?

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.678
- It varies, I mean, I
usually tell the guys

00:00:49.678 --> 00:00:51.052
- What do you mean, you
say I love you guys.

00:00:51.052 --> 00:00:52.437
- Yeah, I say I love you guys, and.

00:00:52.437 --> 00:00:54.172
- You're the emotional
one, I love you Danny.

00:00:54.172 --> 00:00:55.173
- No I'm not, I'm not.

00:00:55.173 --> 00:00:56.116
- I love you guys.

00:00:56.116 --> 00:00:57.129
- Yes.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:00:59.860
- And then we all put our mics to Joey,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.375
and Joey will give us usually one word,

00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:04.170
one word of inspiration,

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.480
and it could be anything
pertaining to anything.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.313
- Yeah.

00:01:07.313 --> 00:01:08.146
- I love the words that just

00:01:08.146 --> 00:01:08.979
popped in my head that I was

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:10.800
hoping you'd say, but I can't say now.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.515
- Tell me, it'll be opening
night at the Mixtape Tour

00:01:14.515 --> 00:01:16.400
- Just random, just,
yeah I'm not gonna do it.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.233
- Yeah.

00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:18.066
- So not classy.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:19.963
What about you, Rick?

00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:21.750
You have anything you do before show,

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:22.940
do you Rick roll yourself.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:23.773
- Oh yeah, baby.

00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:26.600
We, we definitely, we, I, we,

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.930
my band, my crew and everybody,

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.930
we get together, we have a shot of Jager.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:30.823
- Oh, wow.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.767
- Okay, yeah.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:36.944
Bringing the rock and roll
to Mixtape Tour, alright.

00:01:36.944 --> 00:01:38.427
- And then, and then,

00:01:38.427 --> 00:01:39.960
I'm going to curse a little on here now,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.680
So if there's any children watching,

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.569
cover their ears.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.402
- Earmuffs.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.235
- And we look each other in the eye

00:01:44.235 --> 00:01:45.068
and we say,

00:01:45.068 --> 00:01:46.850
oh my God, that was strong.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:47.683
And we say,

00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:49.383
have a good (Beep) show,

00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:50.310
and the reason we do that

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.480
is because because I don't want anybody

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.720
to ever walk on the stage

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.642
thinking that we've got this.

00:01:53.642 --> 00:01:57.990
I like everybody including
me to walk up there thinking

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:58.823
we've got to work for this.

00:01:58.823 --> 00:01:59.656
Do you know what I mean?

00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:00.489
- Yeah

00:02:00.489 --> 00:02:01.322
- Yes

00:02:01.322 --> 00:02:02.155
- In someone's mind they go.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:02.988
- Yeah

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.517
- Yeah man

00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:05.607
- And then it breaks the nerves down.

00:02:05.607 --> 00:02:07.740
I usually look at one of my band members

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.573
and be like

00:02:08.573 --> 00:02:09.727
"Lester don't (Beep) this up for us"

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.360
- That's usually what I do.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.280
- You're welcome.

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:18.353
I like to be as supportive as possible.

